 "caveat": "The spatial hold-out is not fully independent: NASA POWER temperature cells are about 0.5 degrees, and all 4 held-out points share a cell with at least one training point (the same cell series; since the lapse-rate correction each point has its own elevation and shifted temperatures, so the shared part is the cell's temperature and humidity pattern, not identical numbers): gualan (with chiquimula, jocotan, zacapa); sanarate (with guastatoya); asuncionmita (with jutiapa, santacatarinamita, jalapa, monjas, cuilapa); rabinal (with sanmartin, salama, cubulco). Rainfall (ERA5) and, for some points, solar radiation still differ, but temperature and humidity are shared. Use bySplit.testYears (temporal hold-out at non-held-out points) as the cleanest generalization estimate; testPoints and testBoth mix both effects. Task 13e's features were designed after seeing Task 13d's test R²; the models were never fit on test rows, but test results steered one design round."
}